    "body": "This is no different that other history attributes (i.e., history.state) and methods (e.g., history.pushState()). \n\nI am not exactly sure what \"window.history object from domain A is stored somewhere\" means.\n\nI have a small test where I navigate an iframe and try to keep a reference to its history object (top frame and iframe should be same origin). Updating state, or scrollRestoration after navigation using the old reference does not see to affect the current document at all.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
