    "created_at": "2015-11-19T00:03:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-11-19T00:03:59Z",
    "body": "window.history is bound  to document (well, possibly not quite exactly in case of initial about:blank, it should be probably bound to Window object [note, not WindowProxy!]) sure, but the spec talks about \n\"current entry in the session history.\".  And \"The sequence of Documents in a browsing context is its session history\". So scrollRestoration ends up changing whatever entry is the current entry in the session history, regarding whether .history object's document is the current document in browsing context.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
